<h2 id="notation">Notation and definitions</h2>
<p>All symbols used in the derivations are defined in Table 1 at or before first use. Molar flow rates carry the unit mol/s. Compositions are mole fractions and are dimensionless. The light key, abbreviated LK, is the component whose separation between the two products is specified and which is recovered predominantly in the distillate. The heavy key, abbreviated HK, is the component whose separation between the two products is specified and which is recovered predominantly in the bottoms. In a binary mixture the light key is the more volatile component and the heavy key is the less volatile component.</p>
