<h2 id="limits">The two limits as bounds on design, and summary</h2>
<p>The two derivations bound the feasible design region from opposite sides. The Fenske result holds the separation fixed and minimises the stage count, at the cost of infinite reflux. The Underwood result holds the separation fixed and minimises the reflux ratio, at the cost of an infinite stage count. A real column operates with a finite stage count greater than the minimum stage count and a finite reflux ratio greater than the minimum reflux ratio. The empirical correlation of Gilliland [6] interpolates between the two limits and estimates the stage count at a specified finite reflux ratio, or the reflux ratio at a specified finite stage count; the combination of the Fenske equation, the Underwood equations, and the Gilliland correlation constitutes the standard shortcut design sequence, used for initial sizing and for initial estimates in rigorous stage-by-stage calculation [4, 5].</p>
<div class="summarybox">
<p>Fenske equation (minimum stages at total reflux; constant relative volatility; reboiler counted as one stage): \(N_{\min} = \ln \left[ \left( x_{D,\mathrm{LK}}/x_{D,\mathrm{HK}} \right) \left( x_{B,\mathrm{HK}}/x_{B,\mathrm{LK}} \right) \right] / \ln \alpha\), with the stage-averaged relative volatility of Eq. (15) replacing the constant relative volatility when the relative volatility varies.</p>
<p>Underwood equations (minimum reflux at an infinite number of stages; constant molar overflow; constant relative volatilities with the heavy key as reference component): first solve \(\sum_{i=1}^{C} \alpha_{i} z_{F,i}/(\alpha_{i} - \theta) = 1 - q\) for the Underwood parameter, selecting the root between the relative volatility of the heavy key and the relative volatility of the light key; then evaluate \(R_{\min} + 1 = \sum_{i=1}^{C} \alpha_{i} x_{D,i}/(\alpha_{i} - \theta)\).</p>
<p>Worked example (relative volatility 2.50, feed mole fraction of the light key 0.50, distillate mole fraction of the light key 0.95, bottoms mole fraction of the light key 0.05, saturated liquid feed): minimum stage count 6.43 including the reboiler; Underwood parameter 1.429; minimum reflux ratio 1.10, confirmed by the binary graphical construction and by the stripping pinch relation.</p>
</div>

